WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.533 --> 00:00:15.875
one really cool thing about our apartment.

2
00:00:16.876 --> 00:00:19.338
Well, actually, there are two really cool things.

3
00:00:20.358 --> 00:00:24.721
The first cool thing is my bedroom, where I do most of my inventing.

4
00:00:25.722 --> 00:00:27.884
The second cool thing is our fireplace.

5
00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:31.429
Most apartment buildings don't have fireplaces.

6
00:00:32.469 --> 00:00:36.430
But our building is really old, and there are lots of fireplaces.

7
00:00:38.431 --> 00:00:39.911
We have one in our living room.

8
00:00:41.892 --> 00:00:47.874
Shortly after Tate stopped yelling at me for taking the last granola bar, my mom came home from

9
00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:51.255
work. It was raining outside.

10
00:00:52.075 --> 00:00:54.236
Thunder boomed and lightning flashed.

11
00:00:57.644 --> 00:01:01.127
"This is a good night to make a fire," my mom said.

12
00:01:02.208 --> 00:01:05.110
So after dinner my mom built a fire in the fireplace.

13
00:01:06.472 --> 00:01:08.353
Molly, Josh, and Jenny came over.

14
00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:12.257
We all sat on the rug in front of the crackling fire.

15
00:01:13.237 --> 00:01:16.140
We played cards while the rain beat against the windows.

16
00:01:19.363 --> 00:01:20.764
Soon Molly fell asleep.

17
00:01:21.825 --> 00:01:25.368
She still wasn't getting much sleep because of bad dreams about monsters.

18
00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:28.982
We let Molly sleep and played cards without her.

19
00:01:36.367 --> 00:01:40.390
I was getting sleepy myself when I heard the wail of a fire engine.

20
00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:44.392
Then came the sound of a smoke detector in our building.

21
00:01:46.554 --> 00:01:47.654
Molly woke up suddenly.

22
00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:49.776
"Is the apartment on fire?"

23
00:01:50.256 --> 00:01:50.817
she cried.

24
00:01:50.837 --> 00:01:53.218
"No," my mom said.

25
00:01:53.238 --> 00:01:55.440
"Everything is fine here."

26
00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:59.181
I glanced at the fire in our fireplace.

27
00:02:00.601 --> 00:02:02.041
The fire was almost out.

28
00:02:03.482 --> 00:02:06.823
But the sound of the siren was really close now.

29
00:02:08.763 --> 00:02:10.764
I ran to our front windows and looked out.

30
00:02:10.784 --> 00:02:15.925
"The fire truck stopped in front of our building!"

31
00:02:16.305 --> 00:02:16.845
I cried.

32
00:02:16.865 --> 00:02:19.706
"And the firefighters are jumping out!"

33
00:02:20.726 --> 00:02:22.027
My mom looked alarmed.

34
00:02:22.047 --> 00:02:25.508
"Uh-oh. We'd better get out of the building fast!"

35
00:02:25.868 --> 00:02:26.368
she said.

36
00:02:27.284 --> 00:02:31.566
Most of the people who lived in our building were already standing outside on the sidewalk.

37
00:02:32.507 --> 00:02:36.109
Mr. Chen was there, and Molly's mom and dad were there with Caswell.

38
00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.691
They rushed over and gave Molly a hug.

39
00:02:39.711 --> 00:02:44.854
"I called the fire department," said Molly's dad.

40
00:02:44.874 --> 00:02:47.235
"Our TV exploded!"

41
00:02:48.336 --> 00:02:50.097
Most little kids would be scared.

42
00:02:50.977 --> 00:02:52.018
But not Caswell!

43
00:02:52.598 --> 00:02:55.440
Instead he was grinning and looking pretty excited.

44
00:02:56.524 --> 00:02:59.346
"There was a big bang and lots of smoke!"

45
00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:04.430
We watched the firefighters enter the buidling.

46
00:03:05.771 --> 00:03:09.273
They were wearing special helmets and carrying long hoses.

47
00:03:10.414 --> 00:03:12.115
Soon they came outside again.

48
00:03:13.516 --> 00:03:15.477
One was carrying Molly's TV.

49
00:03:15.497 --> 00:03:20.161
"Everything is fine," the firefighter told Molly's parents.

50
00:03:20.181 --> 00:03:24.704
"Except for your TV," added another firefighter.

51
00:03:25.836 --> 00:03:27.697
"I guess you'll need to buy a new one."

52
00:03:27.717 --> 00:03:34.358
"Maybe one of the monsters from Monster Madness made it explode," said Caswell.

53
00:03:35.559 --> 00:03:37.439
The first firefighter laughed.

54
00:03:37.459 --> 00:03:42.161
"I don't think that was the reason," he said.

55
00:03:42.181 --> 00:03:45.582
"The fire was probably caused by the lightning."

56
00:03:45.602 --> 00:03:48.222
"Thank goodness we're all safe!"

57
00:03:48.763 --> 00:03:49.243
said Mrs.

58
00:03:49.343 --> 00:03:53.544
O'Donnell. I noticed that Molly didn't look sleepy anymore.

59
00:03:54.864 --> 00:03:55.725
She looked happy.

60
00:03:56.245 --> 00:03:59.948
Just before we all went back inside, she leaned over to me.

61
00:03:59.968 --> 00:04:02.810
"Iggy," she whispered.

62
00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:06.672
"This is the best thing that ever happened!"

63
00:04:06.692 --> 00:04:09.554
"The fire truck coming to our building?"

64
00:04:09.974 --> 00:04:10.995
I said in surprise.

65
00:04:11.015 --> 00:04:13.917
"No," said Molly.

66
00:04:13.937 --> 00:04:16.919
"My family's TV exploding."

67
00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:18.640
She grinned.

68
00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:23.884
"No more watching Monster Madness after school every day!"

69
00:04:25.336 --> 00:04:26.056
I nodded.

70
00:04:26.076 --> 00:04:31.878
I hadn't invented anything to solve Molly's problem, but it had solved itself.

71
00:04:33.078 --> 00:04:36.139
Molly didn't have to worry about scary monster shows anymore.

72
00:04:37.159 --> 00:04:39.900
Molly's parents left the TV sitting out on the curb.

73
00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:43.881
"Good-bye, TV!"

74
00:04:44.341 --> 00:04:45.402
said Molly happily.

75
00:04:47.622 --> 00:04:49.803
There was one thing she didn't expect though.

76
00:04:51.103 --> 00:04:53.964
Her mom and dad bought another TV the next day!

77
00:04:57.729 --> 00:05:01.395
So Caswell and Lucy went back to watching Monster Madness.

78
00:05:02.497 --> 00:05:05.402
And poor Molly went back to not sleeping.
